# Manual matches the app (source of truth = the app)

Owner rule: **always keep the user manual and in-app guides matching what the app actually does and shows**, so drivers/managers are never misled.

## When app behaviour or UI copy changes

If a change alters a user-visible function, flow, button label, screen name, or a
"why you can't do X" behaviour, update the docs in the **same change**:

- **Driver manual (canonical):** `app-next/docs/user-guides/driver-ui-guide-esl.md`
- **In-app driver guide (pictures):** `app-next/src/components/guides/DriverGuideArticle.tsx`
- **In-app "How your record works":** `app-next/src/app/driver/help/page.tsx`
- **Manager manual:** `app-next/docs/user-guides/manager-ui-guide.md` and `ManagerGuideArticle.tsx`

The app is the source of truth. The manual/guides change to match the app — not the reverse — unless the owner explicitly asks to change behaviour.

## Prefer shared constants over hardcoded copy

When a guide describes a button/label that exists as a constant, reference the
constant so the guide can never drift.

```tsx
// ❌ BAD — will silently drift from the real button
["Produce roadside PDF", "One PDF for a regulator"]

// ✅ GOOD — tracks the actual on-screen label
import { ROADSIDE_PRODUCE_BUTTON_LABEL } from "@/lib/roadside-pdf";
[ROADSIDE_PRODUCE_BUTTON_LABEL, "One PDF for a regulator"]
```

## Do not describe removed features

If a feature is removed (e.g. the driver alertness "How alert do you feel?"
dropdown), remove it from every manual/guide too. Never leave stale steps.
